# keel-overlay-etcd: etcd is disabled in a simple installation of Keel
# Core (handbook decision 0041). Debian's presets enable every unit they do
# not name, and systemd applies them on a first boot, when /etc/machine-id
# is missing or says "uninitialized", and on `systemctl preset-all`:
# without this line either would enable etcd. keel spec apply enables it
# where the instance spec says so. See packages/README.md in
# Keel-Linux/common.
disable etcd.service
